{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Yovel, it is the fiftieth year.</b> What does this tell? Since it says ״וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם״ and so forth, as is in Rosh Hashanah (8a) and in Targum [Onkelos]." "<b>Its nezer.</b> The guarded grapes — but you may harvest from what is ownerless. Just as is said regarding the seventh year, so is said regarding Yovel. It turns out that two holy years are adjacent to each other — the forty-ninth year is shemittah, and the fiftieth year is Yovel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:15.081507749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}